            "result_text": "Done! I've created the `run_tasks` function in `/app/run.py` with the following features:\n\n**Implementation details:**\n- Uses `asyncio.Semaphore` to enforce the `max_concurrent` limit\n- Wraps each task callable so it acquires the semaphore before running\n- On `KeyboardInterrupt`: cancels tasks that haven't started yet, then waits for all running tasks to complete (allowing their cleanup code in finally blocks to run), then re-raises the interrupt\n\n**How it works:**\n1. Tasks are created upfront with `asyncio.create_task()`\n2. First `gather()` runs them with concurrency control via semaphore\n3. If `KeyboardInterrupt` occurs, any pending tasks are cancelled\n4. Second `gather()` waits for all tasks to finish (currently running ones complete with cleanup)\n5. The interrupt is re-raised\n\nThe tests confirm it correctly limits concurrency to 3 tasks, runs cleanup code even when interrupted, and can be imported as `from run import run_tasks`."
